Alex here with a gamespot news update  did you ever wonder why digital games on  consoles stay more expensive than their  physical counterparts Ubisoft recently  shed a little light on this subject  during a post earnings conference call  question and answer session Ubisoft was  asked about the disparity Ubisoft CEO is  gman said digital is more reactive than  what we put in stores but at the same  time it doesn't react as fast on  consoles than it does on PC where we can  say is that when games are older than  one year digital is a lot more dynamic  on console because there are less units  and stores it's a new business a new  trend and we think all this will get  more in line with time but for sure at  the moment you see all sorts of prices  depending on who is doing a promotion  for that specific week an example of  this pricing is far cry 4 the first  person shooter still sells with 60 bucks  on PSN even though you can pick it up on  amazon for twenty four dollars on any  given day piemonte also pointed to one  other factor that needs to be taken into  account which is how many copies of a  particular game are left on store  shelves you said one thing to consider  is related to stocks we have stock in  stores we tend to make sure we decrease  the quantity of units and stores before  going digital with lower prices digital  or physical the debate still rages on  let us know what you think in the  comments and for more news keep an eye  on gamespot com  you
 

